# Production build env for the E3 public / coach SPA.
# Vite bakes VITE_* at build time (`vite build` loads .env.production). Without this,
# readConfig() yields apiBaseUrl='' and rest-client fetches RELATIVE to CloudFront, which
# serves the SPA index.html (HTTP 200, HTML not JSON) for every /o*/… path. getEvent then
# returns that HTML string, the render (event.categorie.map) throws, and the route's bare
# catch shows the generic "Si è verificato un errore" card — with no failing network call
# and no console error. (Same footgun the E1 .env.production documents.)
#
# rest-client joins as `${baseUrl}${path}` where path starts with '/', so NO trailing
# slash. This is the stg ApiStack API Gateway stage root (CDK output), matching E1.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://hnvcmo803a.execute-api.eu-south-1.amazonaws.com/prod
